Z||000000||Homicidal||04-26-2000||02:55 AM||||Just curious if this could be part of my clutch problem.  lemme know the test for it if there is one!||||reg||1
Z||000001||mwbackus||04-26-2000||05:13 AM||||Magnetic attraction test.<BR>Also check the clutch shaft lever, the part that you had to replace is a real good indication that the lever has cracked where it attaches to the clutch shaft. When the lever cracks, the slipage results in extra travel that allows the slave rod to pop out of the end cap, and usually destroys it in the process.<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Homicidal||04-26-2000||09:59 AM||||Would it feel like a "soft pedal"?||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||04-26-2000||12:41 PM||||A soft pedal is an indication of air in the line. You may have a leaky master or slave cylinder and or both. As far as a clutch pedal I carry that and also master and slave cylinders. Look on my website in the parts catalog.||||reg||1
